That applies to a person, so it does.

01:05:46.000 --> 01:05:47.000
No’ anyone.

01:05:47.000 --> 01:05:51.000
What did that mean?

01:05:52.000 --> 01:05:53.000
Dour.

01:05:53.000 --> 01:05:54.000
[Mugairean/?].

01:05:54.000 --> 01:05:56.000
Sort of creeping about on your own.
Mouching about and …

01:06:00.000 --> 01:06:02.000
Now, glam.

01:06:02.000 --> 01:06:03.000
Glam - that’s somebody getting a grip of you.

01:06:03.000 --> 01:06:04.000
To grab.

01:06:06.000 --> 01:06:07.000
Glam? Aye.

01:06:07.000 --> 01:06:09.000
Aye, glammin’ you.

01:06:09.000 --> 01:06:11.000
Somebody getting a grip of you.

01:06:11.000 --> 01:06:12.000
That’s right.

01:06:12.000 --> 01:06:13.000
He’s aye glammin’. I’ve heard it.

01:06:13.000 --> 01:06:15.000
He’s aye glamming?

01:06:16.000 --> 01:06:19.000
Aye. He’s a nuisance that fellow, he’s aye glammin’.

01:06:19.000 --> 01:06:20.000
Something to that … you know you would say that.

01:06:20.000 --> 01:06:23.000
I couldn’t be bothered with that fellow- he’s aye glammin’ at you.

01:06:24.000 --> 01:06:26.000
It depends on who it is!

01:06:26.000 --> 01:06:27.000
Christ, aye.

